# Changelog

## 1.3.0
Power upgrade: input protection, a protected 5 V rail and per-slot rail selection.

* **Input protection** at the USB-C connector: **F1** resettable polyfuse
  (BSMD1812-200-16V, 2 A hold / 4 A trip / 16 V) in series with VBUS and TVS **D2**
  (SMAJ5.0A) on the protected node, both upstream of FB1.
* **New protected 5V_SYS rail**, tapped from protected VBUS (after F1, before FB1) with its
  own polyfuse **F2** (MF-MSMF110/16-2, 1.1 A hold / 2.2 A trip / 16 V), TVS **D3**,
  100 uF/16 V + 0.1 uF bulk and an ERC PWR_FLAG. Protection hierarchy: F1 (2 A hold) protects
  the source/wiring, F2 (1.1 A hold) the 5 V branch, U5's own internal limit the 3.3 V branch.
* **Accepted limitation (documented in POWER.md):** the TVS diodes clamp at 9.2 V at peak
  pulse, above the 6 V absolute maximum of the mux inputs and of U5; VBUS_PROT can therefore
  transiently exceed 6 V during a surge. No rated OVP is fitted in v1.3.0; the planned (not
  implemented) mitigation is a rated OVP switch upstream of both branches.
* **12 x per-slot 2:1 power mux** (**U6..U17**, TPS2111APWR, extended part, 2 482 in stock):
  IN1 = 5V_SYS, IN2 = +3.3 V, OUT = the slot rail feeding all five pins of the existing
  `VSUPPLY_n` socket (net `VSLOT_n`). Manual mode (D0 strapped low), reverse and
  cross-conduction blocking. (The input labels are swapped relative to the original brief so
  that the mandated jumper polarity - shunt = 5 V - is preserved; see POWER.md.)
* **Per-slot current limit** `R28..R51 = 750 ohm` -> about 667 mA nominal, inside the
  datasheet-guaranteed 0.63-1.25 A adjustment range of the TPS2111A.
* **Per-slot selection**: `SEL_n` with a 100 k pulldown and a low-profile 1x02 header
  (**J7..J18**, 2.00 mm, hidden under a mated module). **Shunt fitted = 5V_SYS; shunt absent
  or lost = +3.3 V (fail-safe).** Slot current flows through the mux only - the header carries
  the select level, never slot power.
* Per-mux decoupling 1 uF + 0.1 uF on the slot rail.
* **Sourcing**: LCSC/MPN/Manufacturer fields added to every symbol; `production/bom.csv`
  regenerated. The 13 previously `TO-VERIFY` lines are now resolved (verified C-numbers, with
  FB1/FB2 substituted by the stocked 0805 bead CBW201209U801T and C2/C16/R10/R12/J5/SW1/
  sockets/INPUT1/5V14 all identified). Remaining `NOT-JLC` (4 lines, by design, hand-solder):
  the four 3.5 mm jacks and the two RV09 pots; plans recorded in POWER.md.
* BOM values fixed (the 24 slot sockets were mislabelled `Conn_02x05_Socket` although they are
  1x05; the SPICE sources V1..V3 are no longer offered for assembly).
* No LED is added for 5 V indication (module firmware indicates its own rail).
* U5/FB1/FB2 and the 3.3 V regulator are unchanged. PCB placement/routing is NOT part of this
  revision - see POWER.md for the Phase 2 constraints.

## 1.2.0
Introduce a new LDO (AP2112K-3.3) which has an EN functionality.
So, we can implement the reset button without using additional components.

Due the older design with a transitor, it won't be able to load mutiple MCUs.

## 1.1.0
Change the push button to a better one.

## 1.0.0
Release 1.0.0

## 0.8.0
Update a footprint of a resistor, so we use the JLCPCB default parts.

## 0.7.0
Add input grounding & remove line_out input buffering

## 0.6.0
Introduce headphone and line out into the base

## 0.5.0

Introduce a RESET button.
Add large capacitors to handle more power fluctuations.

## 0.4.0
Removed power extension via TRS cables. Even with the regulator it will be noisy.
Now we only support GND syncing via TRS.

## 0.3.1

Update the USB-C socket's copper layer masks for proper soldering.

## 0.3.0
Add USB power support to the base.
When connecting multiple base boards, we are sending 5V & the regulator takes care of stepping it down to 3.3v. This will remove some of the critical noise in the setup.


## 0.2.1
Add two Jack sockets each POWER & GND. So, we can cascase if we needed.

## 0.2.0
Add 3.5mm Jack socket for Power & GND delivery between boards.

* Power: Share both 5V & GND between two boards.
* GND: Share only GND between boards

## 0.1.0
Initial Release
